## Phase 2: Authentication + Personalization
**Goal:** Replace hardcoded user ID with real Google OAuth, add protected routes, and personalize the experience.

### Backend
- Add `python-jose` + `passlib` for JWT
- Google OAuth callback endpoint
- Session middleware
- Protected route decorator

### Frontend
- Google Sign-In button (using `@react-oauth/google`)
- `AuthContext` provider wrapping the app
- Protected `<Route>` wrapper component
- Profile dropdown in sidebar
- Onboarding screen for first-time users
- Logout flow

> [!WARNING]
> Google OAuth requires a Google Cloud Console project with OAuth credentials configured. You'll need to set up a consent screen and get a Client ID. I can guide you through this when we reach Phase 2.

